Ingredients:
- 1 cup all-purpose flour
- 2 teaspoons baking powder
- 1/2 teaspoon salt
- 1/4 teaspoon ground cinnamon
- 1/4 teaspoon ground ginger
- 1/4 teaspoon ground nutmeg
- 1/4 teaspoon ground cloves
- 1/4 cup unsalted butter, softened
- 3 large eggs
- 1/2 cup brown sugar
- 1/2 cup granulated sugar
- 1/2 cup dark brown chocolate chips

Instructions:

1. Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.
2. In a medium bowl, whisk together flour, baking powder, salt, cinnamon, ginger, nutmeg, and cloves until well combined.
3. In another bowl, beat together butter, eggs, brown sugar, and granulated sugar until light and fluffy.
4. Gradually add the dry mixture to the wet mixture, mixing until just combined.
5. Stir in the chocolate chips until fully incorporated.
6. Drop dough by spoonfuls onto prepared baking sheet, spacing about 2 inches apart.
7. Bake for 12-15 minutes or until edges are lightly golden brown.
8. Allow cookies to cool on the baking sheet for a few minutes before transferring to wire racks to cool completely. Enjoy!
