5. Provide support: To prevent damage from cold temperatures, provide support structures such as trellises or cages. This will help your plants stay upright and healthy.

6. Harvest when needed: Once your plants have grown to a certain size, they'll be ready to harvest. Check them periodically to see if they're ripe enough to eat. Enjoy fresh produce from your indoor garden!

